  "The page number «211» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 96», in bold sans serif, underlined. At the foot, the signature «27*» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line. The page has no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the right above the double rule of the first field, in one line of their own, «C 93r, O 148v—149r, N 59v.», the letters raised (L01).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-210 (JP2 0238-0242): «Viginti gradus Geminorum» (L02), «Viginti quinque gradus Geminorum» (L14) and «Triginta gradus Geminorum» (L22), the ascendant at 20°, 25° and 30° of Gemini, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L03, L15, L23); headings and numbers in bold. The heads of the columns of the first field as on p. 210 (JP2 0242, L05-L08), from Gemini to Scorpius, with «Horoscopus» in each and without notes, and «Capricor.» for the «Capricorn.» of the other pages; here L04-L07. The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields.",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-210 (JP2 0238-0242), are a third, a half and two thirds of the last number of the field: 172° 43′ (L13) gives 57° 34.3′, 86° 21.5′ and 115° 8.7′, printed 57° 34′, 86° 22′ and 115° 8′ (L03); 174° 17′ (L21) gives 58° 5.7′, 87° 8.5′ and 116° 11.3′, printed 58° 6′, 87° 8′ and 116° 11′ (L15); 178° 55′ (L29) gives 59° 38.3′, 89° 27.5′ and 119° 16.7′, where the sextile and the trine are printed 59° 38′ and 119° 16′ and the quadrature C's 88° 29′ (L23; note f).",
  "The columns, as on pp. 208-210 (JP2 0240-0242): in Gemini and Cancer the three fields lie within 44′, 43′ and 35′ of the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Gemini for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′), mostly above them, except at 5° of Cancer in the third field (below); at the end of Scorpius they reach 172° 43′, 174° 17′ and 178° 55′, where the oblique ascension from the beginning of Gemini is 214° 10′. The six fields of Gemini grow unevenly with the ascendant: their last numbers are 163° 59′, 167° 45′ and 170° 7′ on p. 210 (JP2 0242), then 172° 43′, 174° 17′ and 178° 55′; from the end of Cancer to the end of Scorpius the second field here lies 31′ to 2° 5′ below the mean of the first and the third.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the other fields and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer at 15° of Leo in the first field (note a, L10: C's 82 against O's 102), at 30° of Scorpius in the first (note b, L13: the 172 of O and N against C's 170; the numbers at the head belong to 172° 42′ to 172° 44′), in the quadrature and the trine of the second (notes c and d, L15: the 87° 8′ and 116° 11′ of C and O, a half and two thirds of 174° 17′, against N's 89° 28′ and 119° 16′, the quadrature and the trine of the third field), at 20° of Scorpius in the second (note e, L19: C's 28 against O's 18, the steps 3° 20′ and 4° 27′ against 3° 10′ and 4° 37′) and at 10° of Scorpius in the third (note g, L25: the editor's 161 for the 151 of all three manuscripts, the steps 3° 57′ and 3° 56′). In the quadrature of the third field (note f, L23) N's 89° 28′ is the nearer: half of 178° 55′ is 89° 27.5′, and the sextile 59° 38′ and the trine 119° 16′ belong to 178° 54′; the edition's 88° 29′, from C, lies 59′ below, O's 89° 38′ 10′ above.",
  "Without variants: in the third field 35° 48′ at 5° of Cancer (L24) lies 33′ and 53′ above the other fields (35° 15′, 34° 55′) and 1° 16.5′ above the oblique ascension, 34° 31.5′, between the steps 6° 25′ and 4° 45′. In the second field 138° 7′ at 15° of Libra (L18) lies between the steps 3° 1′ and 4° 41′, where the column rises otherwise by 3° 48′ to 4° 4′; in the first field 138° 40′ at 15° of Libra (L10) between the steps 4° 20′ and 3° 13′.",
  "The note letter g at 10° of Scorpius in the third field (L25) is printed on the line, in the size of the figures: see the critical note."
